A||||15||JSocha||Snowmobile preference?  Or Hottub? That is today's question...||||9||
Z||000000||JSocha||11-27-2001||10:35 AM||||Okay, wife and I have been talking and are looking at the possibility of either buying 1 or 2 snowmobiles or a hottub.<P>Were staying away from Arti Crap (never was impressed with them over the years for reliability and SKI-DOO, just plain yuck) and primarly looking at either a YAMAHA or a POLARIS if we go for "a" or "pair" of snowmobiles.<P>Under YAMAHA:<BR>For a two-up luxury touring sled, were considering buying one - 2002 Venture 700 (700cc - largest/600cc - smallest):<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.yamaha-motor.com/products/sno/500/02vent7_gray_3-01.jpg"> <P>Or going ahead and buying two - 2002 SX600r single riding trail performance units (600cc - largest).<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.yamaha-motor.com/products/sno/500/02sx600r_blu_3-01.jpg"> <P>Under POLARIS, we are thinking of either buying one - 2002 Two-Up 600 Classic Touring sled (600cc - largest):<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.polarisindustries.com/img/sno/02SNOTWOX600CLASSICTOURING_studxx.jpg"> <P>Or again buying two - 2002 "700 XC SP" (700cc):<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.polarisindustries.com/img/sno/02snoperf700xcsp_studxx.jpg"> <P>Waiting for prices for the Polaris's, however, yesterday when they were quoted, they were generally running the same price range for the touring and performance sleds between YAMAHA and POLARIS.<P>Which brand would you choose if it was you between these two brands and why?<P>I've always like POLARIS's myself (parents bought one two years ago and have been impressed versus all the Arti Craps they bought and spent tons of money on) and people I know who have or had YAMAHA's say they typically never go into the shop for repairs and are very durable and reliable.<P>And of course the third option, wife and I were considering was a hottub.  Waiting for prices on that.<P>All of which, we are eventually going to use in our Bed and Breakfast next year as attractions, so it doesn't matter which way we go.  If that makes sense?!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Oreif||11-27-2001||11:25 AM||||In my opinion I'd go for the snowmobiles. I've only been on one snowmobile a long time ago so as to which is better, I don't know. But we had a hot tub, It's not worth it. We had a 5'X 8' tub. Cost of upkeep is high. Always had problems with leaks and heaters going out. We eventually got rid of it. We used it maybe 8-10 times the first year and maybe 4 times the second year. Then it sat for 2 years until we got rid of it. (It was originally with the house when we bought it)<BR>For the cost of one I'd say forget it. <BR>You could always get the snowmobiles and rent a cabin that has a hot tub for a week.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever3000||11-27-2001||11:32 AM||||Celebrity Hot Tub Party<BR>Performed by Eddie Murphy (date unknown)<P>"It's James Brown's Celebrity Hot Tub Party!<BR> And now, here he is! The godfather of soul, and hot tub man number one, James Brown!"<P>Sometimes it make me break out in a cold sweat!<BR>One two three four!<P>Hot tub! Ha! Da!<BR>Ah-full of water!<BR>I say hot tub! Ha!<BR>Day! Ba! Very, very hot...  Very hot! Da!<BR>Hot tub! Gonna get ya hot-a!<BR>Gonna make ya sweat! Hey! Say!<BR>Hot tub! Rub a dub in the hot tub!<BR>Rub a dub with me!<P>Should I get in the hot tub?<BR>(Yeah!)<BR>Will it make me sweat?<BR>(Yeah!)<BR>Should I get in the hot tub?<BR>(Yeah!)<BR>Will it make me wet?<BR>(Yeah!)<BR>Well, well, well...<P>Hot tub! Ah!<BR>Get in!<BR>Gonna get in the water!<BR>Gonna make me sweat! Ah!<BR>Here I go in the hot tub!<P>HHHHIIIGGGHH!!<P>Too hot in the hot tub! Ma!<BR>Burn myself!<BR>Make it cooler!<BR>Good God!<BR>Gonna make me...<P>I'm gonna get in the hot tub..<BR>I'm gonna get in the hot tub..<BR>I'm gonna get in the hot tub..<BR>Ha! Lilin! Lidilin! Eh!<BR>A gonna make me sweat-ah!<BR>Dah! Gonna make me sweat!<BR>Gonna make me sweat-ah!<BR>Dah! Gonna get me in the hot tub!<BR>I can't stand it!<BR>Here I go!  I can't stand it!<P>Here I go in the hot tub!<BR>Gonna get in the hot tub!<BR>Gonna get it wet-ah!<BR>Good God!<BR>HHHIIIIGGHHH!! Ha!<BR>Good God!<BR>Rub a dub!<BR>In the hot tub!<BR>Rub a dub with me!<BR>Good God!<BR>Rub a dub in the hot tub!<BR>Gonna set me free!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steve Normington||11-27-2001||11:35 AM||||How about a two-person snowmobile and a large bathtub with built-in jets? That way the people at the B&B could warm up in the tub after a long day in the snow.<P>If I have to pick one, I go with the Yamaha Venture. I have no idea about reliability, but it is prettier. I think a two-person tourer would be better (and safer) that two one-person sports snowmobiles.||||reg||1
Z||000004||chester||11-27-2001||11:40 AM||||I'd go for the hot tub if you have a nice deck to put it on.  Privacy always helps with those things as well!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">     <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000005||JSocha||11-27-2001||12:18 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR><B>How about a two-person snowmobile and a large bathtub with built-in jets? That way the people at the B&B could warm up in the tub after a long day in the snow.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I just did some price checking again as I had to add some options to the YAMAHA that were optional on the SX600r (Electric start, reverse and mirrors).  I'm at the same price as the VENTURE 700 now.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  So got me to thinking.  And of course "THINKING IS BAD".   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If we buy two VENTURE 700's at the same price as two SX600r's, and since we are already going to have two out of five large bedrooms complete with Jacuzzi bathtubs in our BnB, we can rent out the snowmobiles and upto 4 people can go out riding instead of just two as would be the case on the other units. But that is still open.<P>Of course, later on we are going to be purchasing a Horse Drawn Carriage for the sumer as well a Horse Drawn Winter Sled, of course for winter, as well for attractions to our BnB (I'll post pics of those later).  But that is a much later purchase.  Already have them picked out though.  Winter sled sure is nice though<P>BTW, here is a sample of our Bed and Breakfast website that I've been working on.  Its not complete, some wording on square feet for the bedrooms is guestimates  and this one is only temporary because of the wording ("We will" will eventually be replaced with "We have"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">), but close to what the finished site will look like during our construction phase and then afterwards after rewording it:<P><A HREF="http://www.rugbymfg.com/sfbnb/" TARGET=_blank>The Socha Family Bed and Breakfast</A><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> EDIT:  Changed link and copied my web pages onto our webserver here at work because my brother ISP just doesn't support alot of stuff, such as CAPITAL LETTERS and some JAVA scripting.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Its better now!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 11-27-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000006||Jaygee79||11-27-2001||12:27 PM||||go for the hot tub  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Jaime<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79   ICQ: 85931334</FONT><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jaygee79sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||loafer87gt||11-27-2001||02:36 PM||||I have a Massey Ferguson Ski Wizz and a Johnson Golden Ghost up for grabs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The Golden Ghost weighs about a ton and even has reverse. The thing screams out POS! <P>Personally, I would go with the hot tub. Winter hot tub parties are a blast, and the weather being as screwy as it has lately I would hate to dump a bunch of money on a sled that you can't ride. LAst year we had about a grand total of 1 feet of snow, and nobody got their sleds out.||||reg||1
Z||000008||JSocha||11-27-2001||03:20 PM||||Here were the horse drawn carriages I talked about in my post above.<P><u>Spring to Fall Carriage:</u><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.coyaltix.com/gfx/CA34.jpg"> <P><u>Winter Sleigh:</u><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.coyaltix.com/gfx/22a.jpg"> <P>Wife and I were considering on putting this one inside the BnB when not being used as a conversation piece.<P>Anyways, sorry...||||reg||1
Z||000009||Brian87egotrip||11-27-2001||03:34 PM||||yamaha.  very reliablr/ Had a yamaha jet ski never any probs.  All my boats have had yamaha motors. Never any prob.  YAMAHA.<P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT<BR>http://floridafieros.org/daytona<BR>2002||||reg||1
Z||000010||Brandon86SE||11-27-2001||03:55 PM||||First of all, it looks like a sweet BnB.  I've stayed in 'em before, and it's MUCH nicer than in a hotel or anything else.  Looks to be a nice, quaint place, and not too far away for us Canadians.  So kudos on that, and I'll definitely keep that in mind for future getaways.<P>Secondly, if you're gonna get both in the long run anyways, get the snowmobiles first.  You can charge to rent out the snowmobiles, but I don't expect you'll charge to have people in the hottub.  I would personally prefer the hottub, but fiscally, I think it makes more sense to get them the other way around.  Hot tubs are great, my parents have one, and I'm in it pretty well every night when I visit.  It's great to sit in and watch the stars, or northern lights, and just chat with buddies, or that special someone.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>So I hope that helps!<P>Brandon||||reg||14
Z||000011||JSocha||11-27-2001||04:12 PM||||Yeah, as of this afternoon, we are leaning towards buying two snowmobiles as well.  I'm just waiting for the POLARIS literature and the quotes to arrive on those.<P>My folks had/still have a hottub and we never used it either except a few times when they were gone and the ladies abound came around.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>NAKED HOT TUB PARTIES FUN  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">...Parents coming home unexpectedly early...NOT FUN!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <P>And with my wife, I may still encounter the same problem I did with my parents years ago..."But honey!  I thought you were staying down at your folks with the kids this weekend?!  Have you met Bambie, Denise, or Danielle yet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">?"<P>Anyways, several people we talked with said the same thing about Hot Tubs including my brother who is building his resort.  It sits empty a majority of the time, even though they intended on using it themselves when others at their resort weren't.<P>Only one VENTURE 700 left at the one dealership and I can't find another one in the whole state of ND or in the local region of MN, so he won't be able to trade a unit on his floor for another 700 as he hasn't been able to locate someone either.  <P>However, the same dealership I'm working with who has had the best price so far has 3 VENTURE 600's left where everyone else has only one or none left in their stock and at a much higher price then what he is offering it at and at a lower price the a fully loaded YAMAHA SX600r.<P>But, I'm basically "Snowmobile Nomenclature" challeneged and was hoping others with experience in and with winter sleds and brands could give me a better review of the two brands I'm looking at.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Mach10||11-27-2001||08:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>Here were the horse drawn carriages I talked about in my post above.<P><u>Spring to Fall Carriage:</u><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.coyaltix.com/gfx/CA34.jpg">  <P><u>Winter Sleigh:</u><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.coyaltix.com/gfx/22a.jpg">  <P>Wife and I were considering on putting this one inside the BnB when not being used as a conversation piece.<P>Anyways, sorry...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Since there's already been some parody-song quotes, I'm gonna follow with:<P>Been spendin' all our lives,<BR>Livin' in an Amish Paradise!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Seriously, though, I can see the Dual HDCs as bringing in MORE money to the BnB... But the Snowmobiles are hella fun (If a bit dangerous)<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000013||Uaana||11-28-2001||02:40 AM||||Well I can't speak for Yamaha. But as for Polaris I know that they will bend over backward to deliver outstanding service. If they don't call the natn'l center in MN and they'll hook you up and treat you right. <BR>Have you checked the web pages out for Polaris?<P>BTW yes I do have some interest in this Polaris is a company we work closely with and I personally have gone to the mat for customers in the past and will continue to do so in the future.||||reg||1
Z||000014||JSocha||11-28-2001||11:41 AM||||I'VE JUST DISCOVERD FOR CERTAIN THAT THINKING IS VERY, VERY BAD!<P>Just got off the phone with my insurance agent to find out what it will cost me for Personal insurance and then for renters insurance on snowmobiles.<P>Personal insurance not so bad under my home owners policy.<P>But to consider renting them later as an attraction for our BnB, is just darn right astronomical and unfeasible!<P>Figured it out just to cover the cost of insurance, repairs and maintenance (including gas and oil) and any financing that may be on them, even if used and or fully paid for, I would have to rent out the snowmobiles for between $188.00 to $275.00 per hour, just because of the dang insurance to cover me for liability (which does not include collision and/or damages).  So that idea is out the window.<P>Talked to a dealership in Fargo.  They rent used snowmobiles for $175 to $200 an hour or $1000 to $1500 for a weekend and only a select few people are willing to pay these rates.<P>So now I'm looking at it from a "personal use" perspective.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Got the literature and price quotes on POLARIS lastnight in the mail (and yes Uaana I visted their website  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> which is where I got the pics above from).  Saturday, since the wife has off, her and I are heading up North to look at both the YAMAHA's and POLARIS's, find out who has the better financing and prices.<P>Since I am extremely snowmobile challenged, is there anything I should look at or discuss, other then making sure they have "Carbide runners" under the skies as part of the package?  Liquid cooled versus air? etc...<P>PLEASE HELP ME OUT YOU PROFESSIONAL SNOWMOBILERS!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||1FST2M6||11-28-2001||12:51 PM||||yuou want a real sled.. get a Redline but at $13k base price their not real practicle.<P>we had artic cat when i lived in Michigan.. my dad raced (hill climbed) a kawasaki.  <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redline1.jpg">   <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
